            {
              "text": "In Brisbane’s East and Bayside regions (Carindale, Wynnum, and neighbouring suburbs like Capalaba), several boutique law firms specialize in **Family Law** and **Wills & Estates** and provide flexible pricing models—including free phone consultations, fixed-fee estate planning, and deferred payment arrangements.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Key Boutique Firms in Carindale & Wynnum / Bayside\n\n#### **Connor Hunter Lawyers (Wynnum)**\n* **Location:** 55 Tingal Road, Wynnum.\n* **Areas:** Family Law, Wills & Estates, Conveyancing.\n* **Fee Structure:**\n  * **Wills & Estates:** Transparent fixed fees for drafting standard wills, Enduring Powers of Attorney (EPOA), and probate applications. Estate administration fees are typically settled from the estate accounts once released.\n  * **Family Law:** Offers fixed-fee document packages (such as Application for Consent Orders). For property settlements involving significant equity, they facilitate legal funding and deferred fee structures allowing fees to be paid once property or asset settlements are finalized.\n\n#### **Willwise / Judy Hayward (Carindale)**\n* **Location:** Carindale (by appointment & mobile visits).\n* **Areas:** Exclusively Wills, Estate Planning, and Succession Law (Queensland Law Society Accredited Specialist).\n* **Fee Structure:**\n  * **Fixed-Fee Wills:** Packages are provided on upfront, transparent fixed quotes for both standard wills and complex testamentary trust wills.\n  * **Consultations:** Offers tailored home and office consultations across Brisbane East and Bayside.\n\n#### **Fulljames Law (Carindale / Servicing Bayside)**\n* **Location:** Carindale.\n* **Areas:** Wills & Estate Planning, Deceased Estates / Probate.\n* **Fee Structure:**\n  * **Fixed-Fee Estate Planning:** Operates on an upfront fixed-fee basis for estate plans, basic wills, and powers of attorney to avoid bill shock.\n  * **Estate Administration:** Probate and estate finalisation fees can generally be deferred until estate assets are made accessible.\n\n#### **Duffy Lawyers (Carindale)**\n* **Location:** Carindale.\n* **Areas:** Wills & Estate Planning, Probate, Business Structuring & Trusts.\n* **Fee Structure:**\n  * **Fixed-Fee Model:** High-touch boutique practice offering fixed-fee options for estate planning packages, testamentary trusts, and uncontested probate applications.\n\n#### **Cudmore Legal (Capalaba – Servicing Wynnum, Manly & Carindale)**\n* **Location:** Old Cleveland Road, Capalaba (conveniently located between Carindale and Wynnum).\n* **Areas:** Family Law Specialists (Divorce, Parenting, Property Settlements).\n* **Fee Structure:**\n  * **Free Consultation:** Offers a **free, no-obligation initial phone assessment** to evaluate case circumstances before committing to paid representation.\n  * **Deferred Payment / Legal Funding:** For qualifying property settlement matters, they accept payment upon final property division or partner with family law funders (e.g., JustFund) so you don't pay out-of-pocket during proceedings.\n\n#### **McCarthy Durie Lawyers (MDL) (Capalaba & Cleveland – Bayside)**\n* **Location:** Capalaba / Cleveland (with remote & Brisbane East servicing).\n* **Areas:** Family Law, Wills & Estates, Conveyancing.\n* **Fee Structure:**\n  * **Initial Consultation:** Confidential initial consultations with plain-English reviews.\n  * **Fixed-Fee Wills:** Transparent fixed pricing for single/couples standard wills and testamentary trusts.\n  * **Wills Litigation / Disputes:** Offers deferred fee assessments for substantial estate litigation and family provision claims.\n\n---\n\n### 2. How Fee Arrangements Typically Work in Queensland\n\nWhen discussing billing with these firms, consider how legal regulations shape fee options:\n\n1. **Free Initial Consultations:**\n   * Most boutique firms offer a **15–20 minute complimentary telephone triage** to check for conflicts of interest, review your circumstances, and provide a fixed quote. Comprehensive, in-depth legal advice sessions (1 hour+) often carry a capped fixed fee (e.g., $250–$550).\n2. **Fixed-Fee Wills:**\n   * Basic standard wills generally range from **$450 to $900+ GST** (or $800 to $1,500 for a couple), while testamentary trust wills and complex multi-entity estate plans are quoted higher depending on complexity.\n3. **Deferred Fees (\"Pay at Settlement\"):**\n   * **Family Law:** Queensland lawyers are prohibited by professional conduct rules from offering standard \"No Win, No Fee\" for family law parenting/divorce matters. However, for **property division**, firms can offer an internal **Deferred Fee Agreement** or integrate with services like **JustFund**, where legal fees are paid out of the proceeds of the house sale or asset payout.\n   * **Wills & Estates Administration:** If you are an executor needing to obtain probate or administer a deceased estate, you rarely need to pay out-of-pocket; the firm will usually bill the estate and **defer payment until bank accounts/assets are liquidated**. For contesting a will (Family Provision claims), several firms offer deferred or conditional \"No Win, No Fee\" terms if the claim has merit.",
